              "tag": "h2",
              "html": "What is Quality assurance testing?",
              "s": {
                "ff": "Montserrat",
                "fs": "25px",
                "fw": "800",
                "lh": "32.5px",
                "color": "rgb(0, 15, 35)",
                "tt": "capitalize"
              }
            },
            {
              "t": "text-editor",
              "html": "<p>Quality assurance testing is the process that ensures an organization delivers the best products or services possible. The important thing to note here is that quality assurance does not involve the actual testing of products, but focuses on the procedures to ensure the best outcome.</p><p>QA aims to deliver consistent results by following a set of standardized procedures, which means organizations also must ensure that the processes they use to achieve the desired results are meeting certain quality benchmarks themselves. QA involves all activities related to implementing standards and procedures that ensure software meets a set of requirements before being released to the public. The most important thing to remember is that QA does not involve the actual testing of products but instead focuses on ensuring the best outcome. QA activities are end-to-end process-oriented.</p>",
              "s": {
                "ff": "Open Sans",
                "fs": "15px",
                "fw": "400",
                "lh": "27.8571px",
                "color": "rgb(93, 114, 128)"
